						<div class="p-3">
							<p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p>
							<p class="text-[10px] text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>

			<TableOfContents headings={toc} />

			<h2 id="zhiyuan-overview" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">1. Zhiyuan Fire: What They Actually Are</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Jiangxi Zhiyuan Fire Technology Co., Ltd (branded "Zhiyuan Fire" on its English site) was established in 2019 and is located in the National High-tech Industrial Development Zone of Xinyu City, Jiangxi Province (No. 1488 Guangming Road, Zhiyuan Industrial Park). It publishes a registered capital of RMB 52 million and describes itself as a high-tech fire protection enterprise specializing in <strong>gas fire extinguishing products</strong>, integrating R&D, design, manufacturing, maintenance, sales, engineering and service. It states that its team aggregates decades of fire industry experience — the 2019 date is the company registration, not the team's tenure.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The published range is a coherent gas-suppression portfolio: heptafluoropropane (FM-200) systems, ultra-fine dry powder, hot aerosol, IG541 inert gas, IG100 / pure nitrogen, high-pressure carbon dioxide, fire detection tube systems, perfluorohexanone (C6) and high-pressure fine water mist — targeted at energy storage, wind power, petrochemicals, metal smelting and transportation/logistics, across civil and industrial applications. Its published credentials are substantial and specific: fire product certification from the Fire Product Certification Center of the Ministry of Emergency Management, a <strong>Grade 1 Specialized Contracting Qualification for fire facility engineering</strong>, a fire protection technical service qualification, and a special equipment inspection &amp; testing institution approval certificate (its stated business also includes inspection of seamless, welded and fiber-wound pressure cylinders). It is listed as a National High-tech Enterprise and an AAA-rated credit enterprise in its own materials.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Notably, it publishes a turnkey posture: installation case studies (FM-200 systems, CO2 pipeline networks), a "solutions" section by industry, an active English blog, and a 24-hour inquiry-response commitment. Where other Chinese fire manufacturers sell equipment, Zhiyuan positions itself as manufacturer + supplier + technical service provider — the engineering qualification is what backs that claim.</p>

			<h2 id="wanlian-overview" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">2. Wanlian Fluid: What We Actually Are</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Quanzhou Wanlian Fluid Equipment Co., Ltd (Wanlian Fluid) is a manufacturer and exporter based in Quanzhou, Fujian — the core cluster of China's fire protection and valve industry. Production runs on our own lines, with selected items made by qualified manufacturing partners under an ISO 9001:2015 quality-management system; we state that model openly rather than claiming single-factory production for every SKU.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The published range spans six lines and 45 models, all water-based or water-system equipment: <strong>fire water monitors as a core line</strong> — the <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS series auto-tracking jet suppression cannon</a> with flame detection and self-positioning, plus manual PS series cannons; fire hydrants and pump connections (<a href="/products/overground-fire-hydrant-ss100/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">SS100/65 overground antifreeze hydrant</a>, anti-collision SSFT100/65, SA underground, SN65 indoor heads, and the <a href="/products/iot-smart-ground-fire-hydrant-ss100zn/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">IoT smart ground hydrant</a>); sprinklers and alarm valves (ZSFZ-150 wet, ZSFC dry, ZSFM deluge, ZSFY pre-action, <a href="/products/glass-bulb-fire-sprinkler-zst/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZST/ESFR/concealed heads</a>, ZSJZ water flow indicators); fire-protection and industrial valves (gate, butterfly, check, strainer, digital balancing, and the UL/FM OS&Y line); hydraulic control valves (500X pressure reducing, 100X remote float, F745X water level control, HS41X backflow preventer, EN 12845 suction vortex preventer); and firefighting accessories (extinguisher boxes, hose reels, layflat fire hose, nozzles, Storz couplings, ABC dry powder extinguishers). Our certificate page publishes UL 262/UL 1091 and FM 1120/1130 coverage for specific valve models, CE (EN 12266-1) and LPCB RedBook entries, plus GB-series compliance — all stated per model, with copies on request. Every unit ships 100% shell pressure- and air-leakage-tested, with OEM/ODM, a 12-hour quote response, and the full site published in five languages (EN/ES/RU/FR/AR).</p>

			<h2 id="side-by-side" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">3. Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Dimension</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Zhiyuan Fire</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Wanlian Fluid</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Company / base</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Est. 2019; Xinyu City, Jiangxi (National High-tech Zone); registered capital RMB 52M (self-published)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Quanzhou, Fujian; own lines + qualified partner capacity</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Core category</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700"><strong>Gas &amp; special-agent suppression</strong>: FM-200, IG541, IG100/N2, CO2, aerosol, C6, ultra-fine powder, detection tube, fine water mist</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700"><strong>Water-based fire protection + valves</strong>: monitors, hydrants, sprinkler &amp; alarm valves, water pipeline valves, fire accessories</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fire hydrants</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Not in published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Core line: antifreeze SS100/65, anti-collision SSFT100/65, SA underground, SN65 indoor, IoT smart hydrant</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fire water monitors / cannons</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Not in published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Core line: ZDMS auto-tracking (flame detection, self-positioning) + PS manual series</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Building sprinkler systems</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Not in published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZSFZ wet / ZSFC dry / ZSFM deluge / ZSFY pre-action alarm valves + ZST/ESFR heads + flow indicators</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Enclosed electrical / energy-storage spaces</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700"><strong>Core market</strong> — gas agents where water damage must be avoided (server rooms, substations, battery rooms, wind nacelles, archives)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Out of scope — water-based systems only; portable ABC extinguishers for small-hazard coverage</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Water supply / industrial valves</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Not in published range (system accessories for gas installations only)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Resilient-seat gate, butterfly, check, strainer, bellows seal, UL/FM OS&amp;Y, digital balancing — full water line</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Engineering / installation</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — Grade 1 fire-facility contracting qualification + technical service qualification (turnkey capability, self-published)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Equipment supply; installation via local contractor, with technical support and documentation from us</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Certifications (published)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Fire Product Certification Center (Ministry of Emergency Management) certificates; special equipment inspection &amp; testing approval; National High-tech Enterprise; AAA credit</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ISO 9001:2015; per-model UL 262/UL 1091 &amp; FM 1120/1130 for listed valve models; CE (EN 12266-1); LPCB RedBook; GB series — copies on request</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">OEM / website</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Manufacturer + supplier + technical service provider; English site with language menu; 24h inquiry response</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">OEM/ODM explicit; 5-language site (EN/ES/RU/FR/AR); 12-hour quote response</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Read the table honestly: there is almost no product-line overlap. This is not a fight over the same SKU — it is two different halves of a fire-protection project.</p>

			<h2 id="water-vs-gas" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">4. The Real Question: Water-Based or Gas-Based?</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The first decision in any fire-protection scope is the <em>agent</em>, and the agent is determined by the hazard — not by the supplier you like. Two variables drive it: whether the space is enclosed or open, and whether water contact with the protected equipment is acceptable.</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Open areas, water is fine (water-based):</strong> municipal and industrial hydrant networks, tank farms and depots with fixed monitors, building sprinkler systems per NFPA 13, large process yards. Water is the cheapest reliable agent at scale; hydrants, alarm valves and monitors are the equipment. This is Wanlian Fluid's territory.</li>
				<li><strong>Enclosed spaces, water destroys the asset (gas / special agent):</strong> server and telecom rooms, substations and switchgear, battery rooms and energy-storage containers, archive and data storage, wind turbine nacelles, control rooms. Clean agents (heptafluoropropane, IG541, IG100, C6 — the NFPA 2001 family), aerosol for smaller enclosures, or fine water mist where mist at low volume is acceptable. This is Zhiyuan Fire's territory.</li>
				<li><strong>The fine-water-mist nuance:</strong> Zhiyuan's high-pressure fine water mist is water — but as an enclosed-space suppression system, a different engineering class from hydrants, sprinklers and monitors. Do not confuse "they use water" with "they make water-system equipment."</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Hazard in your project</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Agent family</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Supplier category</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Municipal / industrial yard, tank farm, jetty</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water (hydrants, monitors)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Wanlian Fluid</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Building sprinkler protection (wet / dry / pre-action)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water (sprinklers, alarm valves)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Wanlian Fluid</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water supply, pumping, HVAC piping, backflow</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water infrastructure valves</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Wanlian Fluid</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Server room, substation, electrical panel room</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Clean gas agent (FM-200 / IG541 / C6)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Zhiyuan Fire</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Battery room, energy-storage container</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Gas agent or fine mist, per code</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Zhiyuan Fire</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Wind turbine nacelle, archive vault</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Gas agent / aerosol</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Zhiyuan Fire</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Practical rule:</strong> if the scope document says "hydrant," "sprinkler," "monitor," "water cannon," "gate valve" or "fire hose," you are looking at a water-based supplier. If it says "FM200," "IG541," "inert gas," "aerosol," "heptafluoropropane," "C6" or "battery room protection," you are looking at a gas-suppression supplier. A tender that contains both families needs both suppliers — that is normal, not a conflict.</p>

			<h2 id="quality-and-certifications" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">5. Quality Systems &amp; Certifications</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Zhiyuan Fire</strong> publishes a strong Chinese-market credential set: fire product certification from the Fire Product Certification Center of the Ministry of Emergency Management for its suppression products, a Grade 1 fire-facility engineering contracting qualification, a fire protection technical service qualification, and a special equipment inspection &amp; testing institution approval that also underpins its pressure-cylinder inspection business. If your project is in China, or you want a supplier who can also carry the installation scope, those qualifications are meaningful. For an export scope, the question to ask is per-system documentation: the exact certificate for the exact system model you specify, issued for your destination.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid</strong> operates under an ISO 9001:2015 quality-management system across its own lines and qualified partner capacity, with 100% per-unit shell pressure and air-leakage testing and export documentation coordinated with shipment. Its certificate page publishes UL 262/UL 1091 and FM 1120/1130 coverage for specific valve models, CE marking tested to EN 12266-1, LPCB RedBook entries and GB-series compliance — all stated per model, with copies provided on request. The per-model framing is deliberate: a listing is a property of the exact model you order, not of the company, so the verification step belongs in your PO.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Practical advice:</strong> for both factories, run the same verification kit: certificate resolution at the issuing body's official portal for the exact model, per-unit test records matched to serial numbers, third-party inspection (SGS/BV/TÜV) on a first order, and a sample unit before volume. Our <a href="/guides/how-to-verify-chinese-valve-supplier/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Chinese supplier verification guide</a> and <a href="/guides/detect-fake-valves-fire-equipment-counterfeits/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fake-certificate detection guide</a> walk through each check.</p>

			<h2 id="where-each-wins" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">6. Where Each Manufacturer Wins</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Zhiyuan Fire wins when:</strong> the protected space is enclosed and water is unacceptable — server rooms, substations, battery rooms, energy-storage facilities, wind nacelles, archives; you want a gas-agent selection (FM-200 vs IG541 vs IG100 vs C6 vs aerosol) from a specialist; the project is in China or needs a supplier holding a Grade 1 fire-facility contracting qualification for a turnkey installation scope; or you need pressure-cylinder-related inspection capability alongside the suppression system.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid wins when:</strong> the project is water-based — municipal or industrial <a href="/products/overground-fire-hydrant-ss100/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">hydrant networks</a>, building sprinklers with alarm valve groups, tank-farm protection with the <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS auto-tracking cannon</a>, or water supply/HVAC valves; you need <a href="/products/iot-smart-ground-fire-hydrant-ss100zn/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">IoT smart hydrants</a> for a connected network; hydraulic water-level control (F745X) or pressure reducing (500X) valves are in the BOM; or you are building a distribution brand in ES/RU/FR/AR markets and want OEM plus a five-language technical site.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>They coexist well:</strong> a petrochemical plant, a data-center campus with a process annex, or an energy-storage facility will typically carry both scopes in one bill of materials — water-based protection for the process areas and buildings, gas suppression for the electrical rooms. The two companies' catalogs do not compete, so one project can legitimately source both.</p>

			<h2 id="which-should-you-choose" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">7. Which One Should You Choose?</h2>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-blue">Zhiyuan Fire</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>Your scope is enclosed-space suppression: server rooms, substations, battery rooms, energy-storage containers, wind turbine nacelles, archives.</li>
					<li>You need clean-agent selection (heptafluoropropane, IG541, IG100, C6) or aerosol from a specialist portfolio.</li>
					<li>The project is in China, or you want a Grade 1 fire-facility contractor who can carry the installation scope.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-red">Wanlian Fluid</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>Your scope is water-based: hydrants, sprinkler systems and alarm valves, fire water monitors, fire hose and couplings.</li>
					<li>The BOM includes water supply, HVAC or hydraulic control valves (500X PRV, F745X level control, HS41X backflow preventer).</li>
					<li>You need IoT smart hydrants, an auto-tracking cannon, or per-model UL/FM-listed OS&Y valves for North American specifications.</li>
					<li>You are building a distribution brand in ES/RU/FR/AR markets and want OEM plus localized technical assets.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The fastest way to decide: search your scope document for two word-families. "Hydrant / sprinkler / monitor / water cannon / gate valve / fire hose" points to a water-based supplier. "FM200 / IG541 / inert gas / aerosol / heptafluoropropane / C6 / battery room" points to a gas-suppression specialist. Both families present? You have a two-supplier project — and that is the normal shape, not an error. Related comparisons: <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-ca-fire/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian vs CA-FIRE</a>, <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-forede/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian vs Forede</a> and <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-american-avk/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian vs American AVK</a>; for the verification and payment controls that apply to either supplier, read our <a href="/guides/cross-border-procurement-risk-whitepaper/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">cross-border procurement risk whitepaper</a>.</p>

